 settings uh public  institutions and private businesses  and not only is there a lack of  state leadership  in supporting those kinds of policies  there's actually active obstruction  in states like georgia and florida i  mean just as an example  in georgia the the university system of  georgia which has over 300 000 students  universities are not allowed based on  what's called the board of regents that  dictates policies to mandate either mass  for indoor classes or vaccines and then  look at a state like florida where the  where the governor is actively  prohibiting k-12 schools from having  mass mandates i mean i mean those are  our policy approaches that are contrary  to uh not only what the what the what  the cdc uh recommends but just basic  common sense public health measures  about what we know will make a  difference  yeah well without passing judgment it  doesn't sound like anything we have in  europe professor harry hyman at the  georgia state university thanks so much  thank you very much  you
 

